            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-PlN3daO4GoH4YMx46v1lD5HlgSh\">Regarding the dominant age groups, individuals aged 18 to 34 accounted for similar proportions on all three platforms, at approximately 29-30%. Meanwhile, the 35-49 age bracket showed more variation, with Twitter having the highest percentage at 40%, followed by Facebook at 28%, while YouTube recorded the lowest figure of 26%.</div>\n</div>",
